        "\n",
        "# Q2) Bertrand's Paradox\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Let a circle :\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "x^2+y^2=R^2.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The side length of the inscribed equilateral triangle s is:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "s=R\\sqrt{3}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Let $d$ be perpendicular distance from the center to a given chord.\n",
        "\n",
        "The length of this chord, $c$, is given by:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "c=2\\sqrt{R^2-d^2}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "We want:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "2\\sqrt{R^2-d^2} > R\\sqrt{3}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "There fore :\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "d < \\frac{R}{2}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus,  the event of interest is A:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A = \\left\\{   d < \\frac{R}{2} \\right\\}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Approach I: Angular Uniformity (Random Endpoints)**\n",
        "\n",
        "By rotational symmetry, fix one endpoint. Let the random chord be defined by $\\theta$, the smaller central angle it subtends.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Probability space**\n",
        "\n",
        "Sample space bounded by the maximum possible central angle:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\Theta=[0,\\pi]\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Probability measure using a uniform density function:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P_I(X)=\\frac{1}{\\pi}\\int_X d\\theta\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Event Evaluation**\n",
        "\n",
        "The length of a chord $c$ given its central angle $\\theta$ is:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "c=2R\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The target condition :\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "2R\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right) > R\\sqrt{3}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right) > \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\frac{\\theta}{2} > \\frac{\\pi}{3}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\theta > \\frac{2\\pi}{3}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Let $A_1$ be the wanted event:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A_1=\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{3},\\pi\\right]\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Probability Calculation**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P_I(A_1)=\\frac{\\pi - \\frac{2\\pi}{3}}{\\pi} = \\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}{\\pi} = \\frac{1}{3}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "{P_I(A_1)=\\frac13}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "**Approach II: Radial Uniformity (Random Distance)**\n",
        "\n",
        "Select the orthogonal distance $d$ uniformly along a chosen radial line.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Probability space**\n",
        "\n",
        "Sample space bounds:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\Delta=[0,R]\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Probability measure:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P_{II}(X)=\\frac{1}{R}\\int_X \\text{d}d\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Event Evaluation**\n",
        "\n",
        "From the fundamental geometry derived earlier, the success condition is strictly dependent on the distance parameter $d$.\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "d < \\frac{R}{2}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Let $A_2$ be this wanted event:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A_2=\\left[0,\\frac{R}{2}\\right)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Probability Calculation**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P_{II}(A_2)=\\frac{\\frac{R}{2}-0}{R} = \\frac{1}{2}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "{P_{II}(A_2)=\\frac12}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "**Approach III: Areal Uniformity (Random Midpoint)**\n",
        "\n",
        "Select the chord's midpoint vector $\\vec{m} = (u,v)$ uniformly across the 2D planar area of the circle $C$.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Probability space**\n",
        "\n",
        "Sample space:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "M=\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : x^2+y^2\\le R^2\\}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Event Evaluation**\n",
        "\n",
        "The magnitude of the midpoint vector $\\|\\vec{m}\\|$ is identically the orthogonal distance $d$. The fundamental requirement dictates $\\|\\vec{m}\\| < R/2$.\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "x^2+y^2 < \\left(\\frac{R}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{R^2}{4}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Let $A_3$ be the successful geometric boundary:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A_3=\\left\\{(x,y)\\in M : x^2+y^2 < \\frac{R^2}{4}\\right\\}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Probability Calculation**\n",
        "\n",
        "The area of region $B_3$ is a concentric circle:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A(B_3)=\\pi\\left(\\frac{R}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac{\\pi R^2}{4}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Evaluating the ratio:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P_{III}(A_3)=\\frac{\\frac{\\pi R^2}{4}}{\\pi R^2} = \\frac{1}{4}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "{P_{III}(A_3)=\\frac14}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Conclusion:**\n",
        "*   **Method 1** assumes uniform distribution of the *angle*.\n",
        "*   **Method 2** assumes uniform distribution of the *radial distance*.\n",
        "*   **Method 3** assumes uniform distribution of the *2D area*.\n",
        "\n",
        "Because these generation methods distribute probability mass differently across the circle they yield radically different outcomes for the exact same geometric event."
