        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. The $\\sigma$-algebra generated by $X$\n",
        "$$\n",
        "  X(t,p)=t.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The $\\sigma$-algebra generated by $X$ is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "  \\sigma(X)=\\{X^{-1}(B): B\\in\\mathfrak B(\\mathbb R)\\}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "  X^{-1}(B)=\\{(t,p)\\in\\mathbb R^2:t\\in B\\}=B\\times \\mathbb R\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "  \\sigma(X)=\\{B\\times\\mathbb R: B\\in\\mathfrak B(\\mathbb R)\\}\n",
        "  $$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. The $\\sigma$-algebra generated by $Y$\n",
        "The random variable $Y(t,p) = (t,p)$ is the identity mapping on $\\Omega$\n",
        "\n",
        "since\n",
        "\n",
        "$$ \\sigma(Y) = \\mathfrak{B}(\\mathbb{R}^2) = \\mathfrak{F} $$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4. Subset Relation and Information Content\n",
        "**Proof:**\n",
        "Take any set in $\\sigma(X)$, which has the form $B \\times \\mathbb{R}$. The Cartesian product of a 1D Borel set and $\\mathbb{R}$ is automatically a 2D Borel set.\n",
        "\n",
        "Therefore, $B \\times \\mathbb{R} \\in \\mathfrak{B}(\\mathbb{R}^2)$,\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "$$ \\sigma(X) \\subseteq \\sigma(Y) $$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "$\\sigma(Y)$ contains more information because it resolves individual points $(t,p)$ in the plane.\n",
        "\n",
        "$\\sigma(X)$ only resolves the temperature coordinate $t$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### 5. Marginal Density of $X$\n",
